# Configuration paths only. Keep the completed file outside the checkout.
# Empty bindings deliberately fail Compose interpolation; this file is not runnable.
# Network/port policy is fixed in Compose: applications stay on the isolated
# internal bridge; only nginx joins the publishing edge bridge. No network overrides.
LAPTOP_POSTGRES_VOLUME=
LAPTOP_ADMIN_IMAGE_ID=
LAPTOP_BACKEND_ENV_FILE=
LAPTOP_ADMIN_ENV_FILE=
LAPTOP_BACKEND_STATE_DIR=
LAPTOP_TLS_DIR=

# Use absolute WSL Ubuntu paths for env/state/TLS bindings, not Windows paths.
# LAPTOP_ADMIN_IMAGE_ID must be sha256:<64 lowercase hex> from the reviewed
# localhost build's --iidfile receipt; tags and remote images are not accepted.
# PG volume mount root must already contain pgdata/PG_VERSION (17), plus the
# final restored dataset and roles. This stack never initializes a database.
# backend.env: DATABASE_URL (postgres:5432, preserved vhhealth login), original JWT_SECRET,
# API_KEY/API_KEY_ADMIN, original FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEY/TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY/
# BACKUP_ENCRYPTION_KEY and any existing KEK generations, MONITORING_TOKEN,
# retained TENANT_BASE_HOST and explicitly reviewed tenant-resolution settings.
# vhhealth_app is the preserved NOLOGIN SET LOCAL ROLE target, not the login.
# admin.env: matching JWT_SECRET, BACKEND_API_KEY and existing private CSRF
# configuration. Do not copy the complete old workload environment wholesale.
# No .env mount, provider/SMTP/Firebase/Google/Twilio/R2/Sentry credentials,
# old DB/Redis/read-replica URLs, proxy variables, NODE_OPTIONS loaders, or
# external integration activation. Database-stored integrations still exist.
# TLS directory: localhost.crt and localhost.key, readable by the qualified
# nginx image user; protect host permissions. No trust installation is automated.
